    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120094 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120094">
        <rdfs:domain>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120005"/>
                </owl:unionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:domain>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b has material basis c =Def b is a disposition or a tendency &amp; c is a material entity &amp; there is some d bearer of b &amp; there is some time t such that c is a continuant part of d at t &amp; d has b because c is a continuant part of d at t</ns1:IAO_0000115>
        <ns1:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">DESIGN RATIONALE - MILD-owned widening of BFO_0000218 &apos;has material basis&apos;. BFO declares that property with rdfs:domain BFO_0000016 disposition, because BFO has no tendency category. MILD does (MILD_120005), and MILD_120005 states that a tendency, like a disposition, supervenes on the physical makeup of its bearer - so tendencies have material bases too. The domain here is therefore the union of disposition and tendency; range, definition and scope note are otherwise taken unchanged from BFO_0000218, with the definiens widened only by the disjunction. This property is deliberately NOT declared rdfs:subPropertyOf BFO_0000218: a subproperty inherits its parent&apos;s domain, which would reimpose disposition and make every tendency-based class unsatisfiable. It is also not asserted by patching BFO itself, because rdfs:domain axioms conjoin rather than union - adding a second domain narrows to the intersection - and owl:imports is monotonic, so BFO&apos;s original axiom cannot be retracted. The relation to the BFO property is recorded with skos:relatedMatch.</ns1:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has a material basis</rdfs:label>
        <skos:relatedMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000218"/>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: &lt;https://github.com/BFO-ontology/BFO-2020/tree/master/src/owl/profiles/temporal%20extensions&gt;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120101 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120101">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120005"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b has tendency t =Def t is a tendency (MILD_120005) &amp; t inheres in b</ns1:IAO_0000115>
        <ns1:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">DESIGN RATIONALE (2026-10-03) - the bearer relation for MILD&apos;s tendency category, parallel to RO_0000091 &apos;has disposition&apos;. MILD makes disposition, role and tendency pairwise disjoint, while RO_0000091 has the range BFO_0000016 disposition; WONT bore &apos;wound infecting tendency&apos; by RO_0000091 (Staphylococcus aureus, Escherichia coli, WONT_120019), which made those classes and MRSA infection unsatisfiable under the import closure (ELK and HermiT). Declared a subproperty of RO_0000053 &apos;has characteristic&apos;, whose range specifically dependent continuant a tendency satisfies, and not of RO_0000091, whose range would reimpose disposition.</ns1:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has tendency</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


